 "about_text": "Shueisha Manga-Art Heritage (SMAH) is a project of the publisher Shueisha dedicated to presenting manga as fine art. Since 2008 the company has been digitally archiving original manga artwork, and it now produces limited-edition fine-art prints—using archival inkjet, letterpress, collotype and other rare printing techniques—supervised by the manga artists themselves. Each edition is registered on an art blockchain network to record provenance. SMAH operates a permanent gallery in Tokyo's Azabudai Hills, opened in 2023, and has presented its artists' work at art fairs and exhibitions in Kyoto, Miami and Venice. Its program focuses on iconic Japanese manga creators, from postwar pioneers to contemporary artists, treating their original drawings as museum-grade artworks.",
